ept", "title": "Integrated care for physical, behavioral, and social needs"}]}]}, {"id": "86ae311f-3804-4cfe-bacf-d618e260ecf1", "type": "topic", "title": "Chronic Respiratory Disease, Environmental Exposure, and Occupational Risk", "description": "This topic connects chronic respiratory disease to air quality, housing, climate, occupational hazards, tobacco policy, and environmental justice.", "children": [{"id": "dd56429d-028f-4e27-a4d7-2bb41848ac6b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Respiratory disease burden", "description": "Students study asthma, COPD, occupational lung disease, and respiratory disability as preventable population problems.", "children": [{"id": "163dd0ac-3483-4aac-95b2-cfe05ba2d0cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Asthma prevalence and exacerbations"}, {"id": "7063dbcb-1553-4a82-b1c0-b08ad760a665", "type": "concept", "title": "COPD, smoking, biomass exposure, and aging"}, {"id": "9a1bd7a4-645b-4cad-b7e7-e258fcd51be3", "type": "concept", "title": "Occupational lung disease and environmental justice"}]}, {"id": "78a030b7-ff63-44e0-9285-28183e8756b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Environmental and climate exposures", "description": "The point is to connect air, housing, climate, and workplace conditions to chronic respiratory outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "4f06ece5-7c8c-456a-b93c-82ec0ac13180", "type": "concept", "title": "Outdoor air pollution, wildfire smoke, and ozone"}, {"id": "db0b63a8-f7a7-4b6e-8830-b7ae72392ffb", "type": "concept", "title": "Indoor air, mold, allergens, and housing quality"}, {"id": "7387d904-fc96-4ac3-9ff9-983ef90c9c04", "type": "concept", "title": "Heat, climate events, and respiratory vulnerability"}]}, {"id": "794b1fea-bcb0-478e-ac48-478c9d48c927", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prevention and management programs", "description": "Learners translate exposure control into interventions at home, school, workplace, and policy levels.", "children": [{"id": "40120c19-50bd-45d8-8cbc-9d41de7f085a", "type": "concept", "title": "Tobacco control and smoke-free policy"}, {"id": "a8fb44fd-00ea-4fc6-afec-3cf49a75410d", "type": "concept", "title": "Asthma home visiting and trigger reduction"}, {"id": "315cd692-1c5c-42ff-821a-c4751219cf23", "type": "concept", "title": "Occupational standards, monitoring, and enforcement"}]}]}, {"id": "02752335-e239-4d06-ba0d-e9309f6e196c", "type": "topic", "title": "Infectious Disease Epidemiology, Transmission, and Surveillance", "description": "This section builds the transmission, surveillance, and outbreak investigation skills needed to move from individual cases to population control.", "children": [{"id": "4548a311-76a7-4b96-9792-f9be79fb1c8f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transmission principles", "description": "This section teaches the core logic of how infections spread through people, places, vectors, and systems.", "children": [{"id": "dbabb614-a00f-4b1f-97eb-d5d10de3bd10", "type": "concept", "title": "Reservoirs, modes of transmission, incubation, infectious period, and susceptibility"}, {"id": "878ea987-9a24-4446-8d78-47c7fecb2cfb", "type": "concept", "title": "R0, effective reproduction number, herd protection, and attack rates"}, {"id": "d954564f-116b-4c1d-9bcb-d55b813969a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Chain of infection and points of intervention"}]}, {"id": "8152d525-827d-4a2e-bb5d-7e7d87147a0f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Surveillance systems", "description": "Students learn how cases become data and how data become public health action.", "children": [{"id": "2596efc5-0b67-4053-a090-25beee9f025c", "type": "concept", "title": "Notifiable disease reporting"}, {"id": "8e78eec3-e972-4d32-b58c-4be8e2934f14", "type": "concept", "title": "Syndromic, sentinel, laboratory, genomic, and wastewater surveillance"}, {"id": "a6c3eb66-7896-489a-bd2a-ef61a8c3ded3", "type": "concept", "title": "Data timeliness, completeness, privacy, and representativeness"}]}, {"id": "e484722c-feb9-47c0-8d90-5e7cc0b10ea7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Outbreak investigation", "description": "The gist is to move from signal detection to control measures using a disciplined field method.", "children": [{"id": "81e2aadd-18a5-4984-91c1-3b34633d291d", "type": "concept", "title": "Case definitions, line lists, descriptive epidemiology, and epidemic curves"}, {"id": "006a594a-0636-4f34-ac81-ce2a49ea2df7", "type": "concept", "title": "Hypothesis generation, analytic studies, and environmental assessment"}, {"id": "407bc069-fbb8-450d-b144-bb223c39f44c", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk communication and after-action review"}]}]}, {"id": "b3b3ff7b-377d-4e96-a0dd-0cc1bbb71bf9", "type": "topic", "title": "HIV/AIDS, Sexually Transmitted Infections, and Viral Hepatitis", "description": "This topic integrates biomedical prevention, testing, treatment, stigma reduction, partner services, and structural determinants in sexual and bloodborne infections.", "children": [{"id": "f9091701-48a2-46e5-ace2-2e631e6d83f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "HIV epidemiology and prevention", "description": "Students learn HIV as a biomedical, behavioral, structural, and human-rights public health challenge.", "children": [{"id": "423c3732-21fc-4e42-9a79-d211afc91c27", "type": "concept", "title": "Testing, linkage, retention, viral suppression, and U equals U"}, {"id": "07b70bec-b786-47a6-8a67-b9aa3764339e", "type": "concept", "title": "PrEP, PEP, condom access, harm reduction, and partner services"}, {"id": "0621e34d-f0fd-44d9-8786-b86b6d233314", "type": "concept", "title": "Stigma, criminalization, racism, and disparities"}]}, {"id": "e314236c-c723-4dc2-87af-a6302021dff0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "STI control", "description": "This subtopic builds practical understanding of surveillance, screening, treatment, and prevention for common STIs.", "children": [{"id": "a67ae164-a756-4dde-8144-f6159ce0435b", "type": "concept", "title": "Chlamydia, gonorrhea, syphilis, HPV, and HSV"}, {"id": "4aea40e1-e678-46ad-bcf4-8f5c4279d7f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening recommendations and partner notification"}, {"id": "19d52939-987d-4746-a396-9cf03ced3796", "type": "concept", "title": "Congenital syphilis, antimicrobial resistance, and prevention gaps"}]}, {"id": "b413af28-e06b-4c36-975d-cce63e3aa011", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Viral hepatitis", "description": "Learners connect vaccination, screening, treatment, and harm reduction to liver disease prevention.", "children": [{"id": "daccc90c-0315-4840-a4ae-f4cd88c53283", "type": "concept", "title": "Hepatitis A, B, C, D, and E transmission patterns"}, {"id": "92a3b121-8f36-4251-832b-1e7c4bd4df11", "type": "concept", "title": "HBV vaccination and perinatal prevention"}, {"id": "bd544b6f-a5e6-4e58-851b-366f30271dbe", "type": "concept", "title": "HCV screening, curative therapy, and injection-related risk"}]}]}, {"id": "5042e2d5-c6ab-4b5c-865a-2e1190145b35", "type": "topic", "title": "Tuberculosis, Malaria, Neglected Tropical Diseases, and Vector-Borne Disease", "description": "This section broadens the course beyond high-income settings and shows how poverty, climate, migration, vectors, and health systems shape disease control.", "children": [{"id": "09312e26-51bb-4a5c-80a3-081392623965", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tuberculosis control", "description": "Students examine TB as an airborne infectious disease shaped by poverty, housing, migration, immunity, and treatment completion.", "children": [{"id": "ad3258d8-0b22-425e-bbaa-61284b5fd3a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Latent TB infection and active TB disease"}, {"id": "67cf06c7-1730-45eb-a5c5-889d30c072d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Contact investigation and directly observed therapy"}, {"id": "5d3297f7-26f0-490e-bf4c-753eeb48d92b", "type": "concept", "title": "Drug resistance, diagnostics, and global control strategy"}]}, {"id": "78999a63-4874-40c1-8616-f26be887b477", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Malaria and vector-borne disease", "description": "The point is to understand how ecology, climate, vector control, and health systems shape disease risk.", "children": [{"id": "d8ac1f4c-385c-4ba1-9b92-594cee860bb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Malaria life cycle, diagnosis, prevention, and treatment access"}, {"id": "be584ef8-09f8-4217-926a-c9b1ea72b7dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Dengue, Zika, chikungunya, yellow fever, Lyme disease, and West Nile virus"}, {"id": "3e15a004-c439-406a-8e27-8dac31382b0d", "type": "concept", "title": "Vector surveillance, insecticide resistance, and environmental management"}]}, {"id": "ec43f769-e412-4435-9449-af7be0194259", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Neglected tropical diseases", "description": "Learners study diseases that persist where poverty, sanitation, climate, and access barriers overlap.", "children": [{"id": "02c25e5c-9260-4bf3-aa99-54e4fc9f7344", "type": "concept", "title": "Helminths, schistosomiasis, trachoma, leishmaniasis, Chagas disease, and lymphatic filariasis"}, {"id": "f8b4a82b-9a90-4180-8fc7-f7be9e7c351b", "type": "concept", "title": "Mass drug administration and integrated control"}, {"id": "4f1e489d-b0a5-44bd-b8cc-14ef3ed5e4e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Water, sanitation, housing, and community engagement"}]}]}, {"id": "179a470a-7390-47c6-8e13-23281b77b1c5", "type": "topic", "title": "Emerging Infections, Zoonoses, One Health, and Pandemic Preparedness", "description": "This topic prepares students to think across human, animal, and environmental systems while planning for fast-moving public health emergencies.", "children": [{"id": "996a4392-2e2c-4499-9bf0-d93065382d0e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Emergence and re-emergence", "description": "Students learn why new threats arise and why old threats return.", "children": [{"id": "d7cba011-8dc0-4d86-90f3-e318a9c8ec9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Spillover, mutation, recombination, and pathogen adaptation"}, {"id": "70d3a68e-dbc9-4de6-be1f-23ed4169305a", "type": "concept", "title": "Land use, wildlife trade, agriculture, travel, conflict, and climate"}, {"id": "8