-2823e8cfbf13", "type": "concept", "title": "Vaccine types, effectiveness, safety monitoring, and schedules"}, {"id": "f5eb119d-92d3-4901-8acc-b8a962f321a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Coverage, hesitancy, mandates, access, and equity"}, {"id": "c11c5be5-9562-4566-ba44-487a7f675605", "type": "concept", "title": "Outbreak control and catch-up vaccination"}]}, {"id": "31f887c7-4466-4cf5-a6f6-8618147f18f8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Infection prevention and control", "description": "The goal is to understand everyday control practices that prevent transmission in healthcare and community settings.", "children": [{"id": "46733478-50b1-4cb8-845e-6f6820304e8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Standard, contact, droplet, and airborne precautions"}, {"id": "ee1beaff-9bdd-4f42-bb8a-5a060c93c59e", "type": "concept", "title": "Hand hygiene, PPE, ventilation, cleaning, and isolation"}, {"id": "18030456-a9e8-419a-861f-f8f77f0015a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Healthcare-associated infections and device-related risks"}]}, {"id": "449cddf1-8c6f-4b0d-be71-93251ca3fea9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Antimicrobial resistance", "description": "Learners examine resistance as a public health, clinical, agricultural, and global governance challenge.", "children": [{"id": "85acf5dd-3b10-4775-aef6-4ceaedba0197", "type": "concept", "title": "Mechanisms and drivers of resistance"}, {"id": "8b14755c-3d85-4f39-a12c-3085f34d8468", "type": "concept", "title": "Antimicrobial stewardship and diagnostic stewardship"}, {"id": "bd118c92-115d-4b19-9101-50c1c986db86", "type": "concept", "title": "Surveillance, policy, and pipeline challenges"}]}]}, {"id": "c3fc9ca6-90c1-47f8-9c88-ef1b7bd0685d", "type": "topic", "title": "Integrated Disease Programs, Equity, Policy, and Capstone", "description": "The final section turns chronic and infectious disease evidence into an equitable, implementable public health plan.", "children": [{"id": "5ab1b3e6-8e91-4ab3-b27f-4549a5fc99e6", "type": "subtopic", "titl